if you were worried that the call of  duty black ops cold war beta was going  to be a repeat of the alpha  we have some good news it isn't let's  dig into what's new  including maps modes and quality of life  improvements  first off this beta will take place over  two weekends  the first phase goes to playstation  owners from thursday october 8th through  monday the 12th  the second weekend of the beta runs from  october 15th through the 19th  and includes all platforms looking at  you xbox and pc folks  the first two days are only for those  who have codes or pre-orders  but the ps4 crowd can play the whole  time the biggest addition to this beta  happens in the second week  and it's called fire team dirty bomb  fire team is cold war's largest mode  outside of war zone and it will include  two maps fire team splits 40 players  into 10 teams to compete in each match  the objective for dirty bomb is to run  around the map collecting uranium and  deposit it at bomb sites in order to  detonate them  detonating a bomb scores points for your  team but also a radiates part of the map  and be warned carrying uranium poisons  players by impacting perks  movement health regeneration and if  carried too long  it'll kill you if you do die fireteam  has a spawn system that is not currently  present in the other large scale mode  combined arms  you can parachute back in on your team  or spawn directly into vehicles  during the first week of the beta  combined arms which is cold war's 12v12  big team battle mode  is adding a new map called cartel and a  new game type called assault  players will start the match fighting  over a center objective and then work to  push the enemy further and further into  their own territory  capturing the enemy's final zone wins  the match each map will have five  capture zones  and tiebreakers will be decided by one  final battle  over the center capture point this  effectively turns each map into two maps  since you may wind up on just one side  or the other for an entire round  depending on which team takes the first  capture point  for those who enjoy core modes and vip  escort good news  the new cartel map is getting added into  the mix and it takes place in the  jungles of nicaragua  activision's blog post teases something  about the map's relation to the main  villain of cold war perseus  but it's unclear if this means map  secrets or if it's just based on a  location from the campaign  which is common for call of duty games  helping out players across  all modes is a new ping system that lets  you tag objectives  loot locations enemies and even score  streaks  there's also a field of view slider for  all platforms and a more customizable  hood  reaching level 10 in the beta will net  you this snazzy type 821 mutual  animosity weapon blueprint  and no it is not an uzi finally treyarch  has teased quote  frequent updates and a few surprises to  take place within the beta  so we're keeping our fingers crossed for  a zombie's appearance but no promises  cold war releases on november 13th so  head on over to gamespot to join us for  the latest announcements  thanks for watching  you
 

